Alembic migrations for the registry and corpus schema.

The database URL is supplied by env.py from the same place the application
reads it, so a migration cannot be run against a different file than the one
the code uses. Set RECOMMENDER_DB to point both somewhere else.

    python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    python -m alembic upgrade head

Migrations run in batch mode: SQLite cannot alter most things in place, so a
constraint change is applied by rebuilding the table. Constraint names are
generated from a naming convention in db/models.py for the same reason --
SQLite cannot drop a constraint it has no name for.
